{#
After a drop on a category tab.

The same shape as thread/status/_move.stream.html.twig, and for the same
reasons — the rows leave, the frame is re-read, one toast names where they went.

The toast earns its place even more plainly here. A category is the one
destination in this interface you cannot go and look at on spec: the tab strip
only renders categories that hold mail, so a conversation filed into an empty
Forums lands somewhere with no door on screen until the strip is next drawn.
Saying where it went is the whole of the feedback.

Variables:
  count     how many conversations were re-filed
  threads   the conversations, so their rows can be removed
  category  the destination tab, for the toast
#}
{% include 'thread/status/_bulk.stream.html.twig' with {
    count:   count,
    threads: threads,
    leaves:  true,
} only %}

<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            message: 'toast.categorised'|trans({ '%category%': ('tabs.' ~ category.value)|trans }),
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
